  "comments": "<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d177ae98d0a0.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d177ae98d0a0.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"200\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d177af414de3.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d177af414de3.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"125\" height=\"250\" /></a><br />\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/63dad530424ca.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/63dad530424ca.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"152\" /></a><br /><br />\nThis was the first colored general circulation coin in the world.<br /><br />\nAlso known as the conspiracy coin, due to the red center, the US Secret Service believed there to be a microchip inside the coin, enabling them to be satellite tracked.<br /><br />\nIn 2005 coin was issued again, this time not for circulation but as UNC in bookmark. Printed poppy seems to be little different than in 2004:<br />\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/62767a14c6b22.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/62767a14c6b22.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"234\" /></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/62767a1f9170c.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/62767a1f9170c.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"228\" /></a><br /><br />\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/62767a3616b0f.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/62767a3616b0f.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"77\" height=\"250\" /></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/62767a41d0f30.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/62767a41d0f30.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"78\" height=\"249\" /></a><br /><br />\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d177ae98d0a0.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d177ae98d0a0.j